WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.080
So a lot of the people that we’ve been interviewing were born in Mossville.

2
00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.440
You’re kind of one of the few folks that . . .

3
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.460
I migrate over here.

4
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:08.780
Yeah.

5
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.200
Who has actually migrated here [laughing] and has been here longer than they’ve been.

6
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:12.660
Yeah. [laughing]

7
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:19.280
So could you talk a little bit about how . . . how you viewed this community when you first got here,

8
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:24.120
compared to, like, you know, being a person who’s been in the community for a long time?

9
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:28.680
Well, I come through here, [like I said?] good job and work at the plant.

10
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.440
And at that time [?] wasn’t playing that much, but I see there was a steady job,

11
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:40.480
so . . . And I’ve been working then until I retired and keep on going, yeah.

12
00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:45.260
When I first went there, I wasn’t making but $1.75 an hour.

13
00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:50.420
And when I left there I was making $24 . . . $27 dollars an hour.

14
00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:55.920
I was getting top pay, more than some of them guys were working operation, I had the seniority.

15
00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:03.960
So they come along and made an offer and all those that had enough time to retire, go ahead on and retire.

16
00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.820
I was only fifty-five years old when I retired.

17
00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:09.820
But I had enough time to retire.

18
00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.120
I said well, I might as well go.

19
00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.140
Yeah.

20
00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:17.140
So far, I’ve stayed here. [laughs]
